DECISION
AR-H132 is POSITIVE
for:
VALUE-GATED DISCRIMINATING INTERACTION CHALLENGE

WITH:
PASSIVE-PROMOTION
AND
TEST-EVERYTHING LIMITS.

Supported synthetically:

- passive residual promotion has high true recall but severe false-state growth;
- independent targeted challenge sharply reduces false promotion;
- challenging every candidate can cost more than the added model value;
- value gating gives the highest tested net improvement;
- value-gated testing retains most total future interaction value despite lower raw recall;
- high-stakes interactions receive priority even when rare;
- permanent grammar growth should require stronger evidence than transient residual suspicion.

Not demonstrated:

- online sequence challenge generation;
- interaction challenge under real resource crisis;
- delayed semantic consequence;
- interaction dependencies;
- challenge reuse across families;
- adaptive state-cost pricing.

